# www

Minimal site generator for RE:INSTEAD games, playable in the browser with
metaparser-js.

## Build

```
make -C extra/metaparser-js      # builds the player (extra/metaparser-js/build/dist)
python3 extra/www/generate.py    # writes the site to extra/www/build
python3 -m http.server -d extra/www/build
```

## Conventions

A game is published when its directory contains `main3.lua` and `icon.png`:

* `icon.png` — card and page image;
* `main3.lua` — the `$Name`, `$Author` and `$Info` header fields give the
  title, the author and the short info for the card; the `(ru)` variants
  (`$Name(ru)`, `$Author(ru)`, ...) win;
* `dsc.txt` — optional, long description for the game page, may contain
  simple HTML.

Games are taken from `data/games` (`--games DIR`), the player from
`extra/metaparser-js/build/dist` (`--mp DIR`), the output goes to
`extra/www/build` (`--out DIR`).

The generated site:

```
build/index.html              game cards
build/games/<name>/index.html game page with the icon and description
build/games/<name>/<name>.zip game archive, <name>/ inside
build/mp/                     metaparser-js distribution
build/style.css
```

The archives are packed with `<name>/` as the top level directory, as
metaparser-js expects for `<name>.zip`; `saves/` and `autoscript` are left out.

The markup lives in `templates/`: `page.html` (skeleton), `index.html` (game
list), `card.html` (one card) and `game.html` (game page). Placeholders are
`string.Template` names, so `$title`, `$cards` and so on are substituted by the
generator.
